                        "entry_id": "922538cb-b243-389f-b800-56fc1e8428c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fait de nommer un groupe de personnes par un nom différent du nom employé par ses membres."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42c68de1-8d26-44d4-a222-e11c441d488d",
                                "sense_id": "88695480-ae7c-3bc2-89f0-e0951e5501b8",
                                "text": "Appeler des Japonais des « Japonais » est un exemple d’exonymie car les Japonais se nomment eux-mêmes « 日本人 » et cela se prononce \\nʲi.hon.dʑiɴ\\."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ecc7baa1-4b2f-426b-a133-6c3464485804",
                        "source_entry_id": "922538cb-b243-389f-b800-56fc1e8428c8",
                        "source_sense_id": "88695480-ae7c-3bc2-89f0-e0951e5501b8",
                        "target_lang_word": "exonymy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exonymy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "052cbb5e-3db2-31be-a628-58d86784e434",
                                        "entry_id": "21c7c8d7-9922-3c2d-bc0d-461693fb2b8e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The use of the name for a group or geographic region by outsiders, as opposed to that by its members or inhabitants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00c9d3eb-15e9-4bcb-86ce-c446756dbe26",
                                                "sense_id": "052cbb5e-3db2-31be-a628-58d86784e434",
                                                "text": "Eduardo Viveiros de Castro (Brazil/Paris) analysed the comparative relation between exonymy and endonymy in lowland South America."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a1ec97b-8a2d-474f-863e-8a88485a5b23",
                                                "sense_id": "052cbb5e-3db2-31be-a628-58d86784e434",
                                                "text": "As such, there arises a symbolic association between endonymy and the firstborn, and exonymy and the last-born, in keeping with the idea that the firstborn represents internal continuity and the last-born represents the transformation associated with exteriority. Indeed, in the practice of name-giving, the names of the firstborn come from the closest kin and from what is \"inside\", whereas the names of the last-born come from more distant kin and from what is increasingly \"outside.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9684eca5-06ea-4831-9aba-ccdab8cad012",
                                                "sense_id": "052cbb5e-3db2-31be-a628-58d86784e434",
                                                "text": "First it will examine the etymologies of the various groups as products of Egyptian nomenclature (exonymy) or indigenous nomenclature (endonymy)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
